</div>
<div style=3D"margin:0px">=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 SignatureScheme algor=
ithm;<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"margin:0px">=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 opaque signature&lt;0=
...2^16-1&gt;;<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"margin:0px">=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 } DelegatedCredential;<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"margin:0px"><br>
</div>
<div style=3D"margin:0px">=C2=A0 =C2=A0algorithm: =C2=A0The signature algor=
ithm used to verify<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"margin:0px">=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 DelegatedCredential.signatur=
e.<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"margin:0px"><br>
</div>
<div style=3D"margin:0px">&lt;mglt&gt;<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"margin:0px">I am wondering if any checks should be<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"margin:0px">performed with the<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"margin:0px">CertificateVerify.algorithm or if any<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"margin:0px">algorithm would be acceptable. Unless I<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"margin:0px">am missing something it seems a weak<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"margin:0px">algorithm can be used - assuming the<br>
</div>
